    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d195">

                <pb facs="0401" n="373" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v23p2/pg373"/>

                <head>195. Letter From the Secretary of State to the
                    Secretary of Defense (Wilson)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d195-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1957-01-10"><hi rendition="#italic">January 10,
                        1957</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Charlie</hi>: I think I mentioned to you that
                    when we were in Paris<anchor n="2" xml:id="d195-f2"/>
                    Selwyn Lloyd told me that economic
                    conditions in the United Kingdom were such that they had practically made up
                    their mind to take the U.K. troops out of Korea. I asked him to delay any
                    decision.</p>
                <p>If you or the Joint Chiefs have any arguments which you think would be
                    persuasive, I suggest that you let me have them promptly. However, I feel that
                    basically their decision has been taken, although no timing has as yet been
                    set.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                    >Foster</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d195-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d195-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 795.00/1–1057. Secret.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d195-f2" n="2" xml:id="d195-f2-content">
                <p>Dulles was in Paris for the Ministerial
                    Meeting of the North Atlantic Council, December 11–14, 1956.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
